# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 serving window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of serving/tp4-s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled
# in by whoever drives the window; every other value is final. ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image and its stop rule.
# A PRE-EVIDENCE gate job: image tp4-stackfix-3 (already built, the validated S3a / V1b / V3 image) serving c2-packed-tp4-gate, the
# traffic profile's env plus the T1/T2 audits and the gate switches, so the UNQUALIFIED attach is allowed. The gate's own code runs
# from the checkout, so a gate-code fix needs no image build. C2_GATE_JIT=record: no four-card warm plan exists, so the first arm
# compiles and its kernel-cache growth is recorded, not judged (V3 did the same). The arms also warm the host's kernel cache.
# G-B (TP2 M9): the boundaries plan: prompts at the extent family boundaries, 8,192 tokens out (the traffic profile's answer room).
# Duration (estimate): 25 min. Stop rule: as G-M1.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-stackfix-3
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_GATE_PLAN=boundaries
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=8192
C2_GATE_JIT=record
